# SukiSU manager installer: init -> shell transition.
#
# Lives here (system_ext platform policy) and NOT in sepolicy/vendor on
# purpose: a rule purely between core types
#   domain_trans(init, shell_exec, shell)
# placed in vendor policy compiles PARTIALLY — the four allow rules land in
# vendor_sepolicy.cil but the type_transition is silently dropped (vendor
# policy may not create core-only transitions). Verified on-device: the
# oneshot service then aborts at every boot with
#   Could not ctl.start ... no domain transition from u:r:init:s0 ...
# and the manager is never installed, with zero logcat footprint.
# In platform policy the same macro expands fully (verified: the merged
# policy contains the typetransition).
domain_trans(init, shell_exec, shell)
